Care has been taken to ensure compatibility with Connect in a number of ways.
1. V1 (backward compatible):
    - Document-level metadata where subject, email-text, and email-scheduled divs can appear anywhere in the document outside the .email div. produces exactly one email per document, in v1 output format.
    - When Quarto is running within an older version of Connect (before 2026.03.0 as a placeholder), the output will be rendered as one email in V1 format.
2. V2 (new): Nested metadata where subject, email-text, and email-scheduled divs are placed inside each .email div. enables multiple emails per document.

New test documents verify this behavior
- [email-multi-v2.qmd](https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli/pull/13882/files#diff-ea772a2a2b14555aedc64308199125733e93f62464bef46302772c889e3e0059) (basic multiple email generation)
- [email-subject-document-level.qmd](https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli/pull/13882/files#diff-9d72c01b6ccb26ab3070301d31bfc046555bcaadf2db180c418513be87afa328) (old, invalid input format still produces v1)
- [email-mixed-metadata-v2.qmd](https://github.com/quarto-dev/quarto-cli/pull/13882/files#diff-fe67d1c53ad906fed980e593974f82432c6951340c6210721200bba8daf5f598) (incomplete, but valid edge cases)

_I recognize there are a number of documenting steps remaining before this can be merged._

Documentation will exist in the Connect docs, since this feature is not publicly supported. Here is the [PR](https://github.com/posit-dev/connect/pull/35725) to make the parallel modification to Connect.

- [ ] I want to consider adding a field that acts as an escape hatch, where users can choose v1, v2, or auto ouptut types (auto being the current behavior)

